From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:56:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-118: the artboard toolbar always in view -- the
 hint never covers it (0.118.0)

WPF keeps the artboard toolbar (zoom, fit, grid, snapping) at the bottom left of
the design surface. Here the hint at the bottom right, when the view was not
wide enough, ran across the whole bottom and covered the toolbar -- its zoom
buttons could not be clicked (seen in a 1100 px screenshot). Now the hint keeps
to the room right of the toolbar (the view without a scrollbar, its padding
counted) and wraps upwards; it follows a resize. The zoom buttons' tips name the
wheel the zoomWheel setting chose, and Ctrl+- / Ctrl+=.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 192, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (976 px: the toolbar ends at 355, the hint starts at 367; + names Alt with
alt, Ctrl with ctrl; a screenshot checked).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
